From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayman <ayman@pipa>
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-xiaomi-pipa: enable the
 DisplayPort controller

The Type-C connector already declares the DisplayPort altmode and the DP
output endpoint is wired to the USB3/DP combo PHY, but mdss_dp itself was
left at its sm8250.dtsi default of "disabled".  Without it DRM only exposes
the internal DSI panel and no DP-1 connector is created, so USB-C to
DisplayPort/HDMI adapters never light up.

Enable mdss_dp so the msm DP controller probes and registers the external
connector.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-pipa-common.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-pipa-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-pipa-common.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-pipa-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-pipa-common.dtsi
@@ -789,8 +789,12 @@ &i2c16 {
 &mdss {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&mdss_dp {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &mdss_dp_out {
 	data-lanes = <0 1>;
 	remote-endpoint = <&usb_1_qmpphy_dp_in>;
 };
-- 
